SUMMARY:A Tribute to Vaudeville at Strasburg Rail Road
DESCRIPTION:Prepare to be taken back to what was once the most renowned form of entertainment in the world. Vaudeville! The year is 1946 and we’ve brought back some of the best performers for a spectacular revival performance. Join Hoagy Carmichael as he hosts the show of a lifetime with world renown artists such as Ella Fitzgerald\, the Boswell Sisters\, and more. Gather ‘round to witness the style that took the nation by storm. This is ‘A Tribute To Vaudeville!’\n\nA Tribute to Vaudeville is complimentary to every train ride ticket on most Friday and Saturday mornings from April until August. Showtimes are 10:30am\, 11:30am\, 12:30pm and 1:30pm and take place right at the heart of the station on the Town Square Stage.  \nBook your train ticket now and come early or stay late to catch the harmonies and swings of Vaudeville!
URL:https://lancasterpa.com/events-calendar/tribute-to-vaudeville-strasburg-rail-road/
LOCATION:Strasburg Rail Road\, 301 Gap Road\, Ronks\, PA\, 17572\, United States
CATEGORIES:Railroad,Strasburg, PA
